# API Contracts

An API contract defines how clients and servers communicate.

It specifies:

- Available endpoints
- Supported methods
- Parameters
- Authentication requirements
- Request format
- Response format
- Error codes
- Version information

Example:

```
POST /users

Required Fields

name
email
password

Returns

201 Created
```

Well-defined contracts reduce implementation errors and improve interoperability.

